<title>UK: Western nickel seen moving to surplus in 1997 -EIU.</title>
<headline>Western nickel seen moving to surplus in 1997 -EIU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The western world refined nickel market is seen moving into an 18,000 tonnes surplus of supply over demand in 1997 from a 24,000 deficit in 1996, the Economist Intelligence (EIU) said.</p>
<p>It saw production rising 66,000 tonnes due to increases in Canada and Europe while consumption gaining only 18,000 tonnes with a rise in Japan being offset by fairly flat markets elswhere, paticularly Europe which will still be trying to shake of the effects of a slack 1996.</p>
<p>Imports from the East bloc will drop slightly, EIU said.</p>
<p>Its world supply/demand balance in thousand tonnes -</p>
<p>				  1997     1996     1995</p>
<p> Western production	  747	681	653</p>
<p> Western consumption	 869	851	869</p>
<p> Net imports from E.Bloc   140	146	174</p>
<p>London Newroom, =44 171 542 7771</p>
